---
/**
 * SectionEmpty — one line, everywhere a listing has nothing in it.
 *
 *   아직 글이 없습니다.
 *
 * ONE SENTENCE, NOT ONE PER SURFACE (lead decision 2026-09-07). The page-by-
 * page variants this replaced ("아직 발행된 평론이 없습니다", "아직 발행된
 * 이야기가 없습니다") are exactly the habit this round spent itself removing:
 * each surface explaining its own situation in its own words. A single line,
 * reused verbatim, is a system message — and a system message is not the
 * publication talking about itself.
 *
 * Used by: the home's three sections, /archive/reviews/, /archive/stories/,
 * /artists/. Two earlier drafts are recorded because both were rejected on
 * review and the reasons still apply: a block describing what the surface
 * WOULD hold (the same self-narrating voice), and a wordless bordered area
 * with a screen-reader-only word (honest, but it gave sighted and non-sighted
 * readers different objects when one shared line does the job for both).
 *
 * NOT used for: `BoardPanel`'s "아직 이 장르의 후보가 없습니다." and
 * `AlbumBox`'s "평론 준비 중". Those are not "this page is empty" — they are
 * the state of one datum (a genre bucket's nominees, one album's review), and
 * `build.finalize.spec.ts` and US-4 AC2 respectively depend on them.
 *
 * R-4 ("빈 껍데기 금지") is still released FOR THE HOME'S THREE SECTIONS
 * ONLY. The listing pages above are not a release: they exist
 * unconditionally because they are in the masthead, so nothing is being
 * shown empty instead of omitted — they simply have nothing to list.
 */
---

<p class="section-empty">아직 글이 없습니다.</p>

<style>
  /* A line, not a block. The earlier draft reserved a card-row's worth of
     bordered ground; with real text in it that would be a box drawn around
     one sentence. --muted on --bg is 7.49:1. */
  .section-empty {
    margin-top: var(--s-16); /* the gap a card grid takes from its head */
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    line-height: 20px;
  }
</style>
